(3936584, 554309, 59031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by routerguy666:</b></div><hr/><i> Suprised this palced so far down the ladder, it''s really a decent shot.  Did you focus on the chest and then tilt up to the face?  The focus problem is the only real drawback to this image (at least compared with a vast number of shots that scored higher).  F1.8 can be troublesome. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I actually have the f1.4 lens, I just happen to set it at f1.8, but yeah I have focus problems with it sometimes. Maybe just user error but it definitely acts differently from my other lenses. I wish it scored a little higher as well but it''s my first submission so I just hope to improve a little every time. I''ve only been into serious photography for about a year so I''m still learning.</td>', 'Originally posted by routerguy666: Suprised this palced so far down the ladder, it''s really a decent shot.  Did you focus on the chest and then tilt up to the face?  The focus problem is the only real drawback to this image (at least compared with a vast number of shots that scored higher).  F1.8 can be troublesome.   I actually have the f1.4 lens, I just happen to set it at f1.8, but yeah I have focus problems with it sometimes. Maybe just user error but it definitely acts differently from my other lenses. I wish it scored a little higher as well but it''s my first submission so I just hope to improve a little every time. I''ve only been into serious photography for about a year so I''m still learning.', '2007-07-25 16:29:01.000000', NULL, 0),
