(3937197, 556130, 41337, '<td valign="top">At first I saw this as only a portrait on human life rather than this particular person. This was probably because his eyes were covered and I couldn''t get the instant gratification of seeing into his soul or so they say. No I had to take the roundabout way to know him by what life has done to his withered body and it''s only then when I truly see him for what he is and not what I want to see had I looked into his eyes.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-25 18:44:11.</i></td>', 'At first I saw this as only a portrait on human life rather than this particular person. This was probably because his eyes were covered and I couldn''t get the instant gratification of seeing into his soul or so they say. No I had to take the roundabout way to know him by what life has done to his withered body and it''s only then when I truly see him for what he is and not what I want to see had I looked into his eyes.', '2007-07-25 19:43:31.000000', '2007-07-25 19:44:11.000000', 0),
