(3938220, 554875, 68504, '<td valign="top">Well done. Just enough of light and dark, texture and void. Oh yes, and good face and expression.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-25 23:42:53.</i></td>', 'Well done. Just enough of light and dark, texture and void. Oh yes, and good face and expression.', '2007-07-26 00:42:02.000000', '2007-07-26 00:42:53.000000', 0),
(3938255, 556622, 68504, '<td valign="top">Excellent bw.  Very interesting portrait: the unusual angle makes this into a real "head" shot - almost a severed head - and makes the viewer really see the face.  Or something like that.  Engaging at any rate.  Hope to see more portraits.</td>', 'Excellent bw.  Very interesting portrait: the unusual angle makes this into a real "head" shot - almost a severed head - and makes the viewer really see the face.  Or something like that.  Engaging at any rate.  Hope to see more portraits.', '2007-07-26 00:54:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3938263, 556074, 68504, '<td valign="top">Great photo, wonderful expression.</td>', 'Great photo, wonderful expression.', '2007-07-26 00:57:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3938281, 554325, 68504, '<td valign="top">Wonderful rich darks combined with crisp focus and clear expression.</td>', 'Wonderful rich darks combined with crisp focus and clear expression.', '2007-07-26 01:03:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3938344, 556836, 44877, '<td valign="top">My goodness. Clearly, the commenters liked your photo and the non commenters didn''t. I don''t think I''ve ever seen such a wide chasm between those two averages. And who in their right mind would give this most excellent photo a 1, 2, or 3 - or a 4 for that matter??? I''m outraged for you and your beautiful talent. <br/> <br/>Me, I love this portrait.</td>', 'My goodness. Clearly, the commenters liked your photo and the non commenters didn''t. I don''t think I''ve ever seen such a wide chasm between those two averages. And who in their right mind would give this most excellent photo a 1, 2, or 3 - or a 4 for that matter??? I''m outraged for you and your beautiful talent.  Me, I love this portrait.', '2007-07-26 01:21:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3938370, 553635, 52549, '<td valign="top">I love this, it''s so beautiful and so different. Congrats on top 10.</td>', 'I love this, it''s so beautiful and so different. Congrats on top 10.', '2007-07-26 01:35:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3938375, 554305, 61961, '<td valign="top">I was one of your two 9s on this.  I''m surprised to learn you touched up the lips -- I thought for sure those who commented on it were wrong.  That''s how youthful lips look!  Anyway, I like the serious look on the boy''s face and the fact you let the blemishes show.  Handsome kid, too.</td>', 'I was one of your two 9s on this.  I''m surprised to learn you touched up the lips -- I thought for sure those who commented on it were wrong.  That''s how youthful lips look!  Anyway, I like the serious look on the boy''s face and the fact you let the blemishes show.  Handsome kid, too.', '2007-07-26 01:40:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3938396, 556797, 66635, '<td valign="top">I don''t like her laying on the American flag.  So-called "artists" will defend it as some sort of artistic expression.  I just find it disrespectful; though I will concede the possibility that if it were extremely well-done and carried some kind of deep message, there might be a possibility that it could be acceptable.  Maybe.  But not this one.  I am not accusing the photographer of intentionally being disrespectful.  I am simply expressing the view that there are some things that are inappropriate to do with the flag and that this is one of them.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-27 04:12:58.</i></td>', 'I don''t like her laying on the American flag.  So-called "artists" will defend it as some sort of artistic expression.  I just find it disrespectful; though I will concede the possibility that if it were extremely well-done and carried some kind of deep message, there might be a possibility that it could be acceptable.  Maybe.  But not this one.  I am not accusing the photographer of intentionally being disrespectful.  I am simply expressing the view that there are some things that are inappropriate to do with the flag and that this is one of them.', '2007-07-26 01:52:11.000000', '2007-07-27 05:12:58.000000', 0),
(3938535, 555882, 47316, '<td valign="top">ohhh boy. "unappealing expression". Ahhh! Like he was supposed to look suave!<br/> <br/>Annnyhow. Strange comments aside. This is a great photo. I love expressions and stories... 2 of the biggest things that draw me to a photo and you have both here. No comments from you! I kinda want to know what this guy was doing! lol.<br/> <br/>Technically I''d probably like to see more on the left side where his hand is chopped. The bw background was not noticable at first but the more I look at it the line is very obvious, perhaps you could have used a more blurry edge or not done a total desat... maybe 70 or 50 percent?</td>', 'ohhh boy. "unappealing expression". Ahhh! Like he was supposed to look suave! Annnyhow. Strange comments aside. This is a great photo. I love expressions and stories... 2 of the biggest things that draw me to a photo and you have both here. No comments from you! I kinda want to know what this guy was doing! lol. Technically I''d probably like to see more on the left side where his hand is chopped. The bw background was not noticable at first but the more I look at it the line is very obvious, perhaps you could have used a more blurry edge or not done a total desat... maybe 70 or 50 percent?', '2007-07-26 03:20:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3938542, 556844, 47316, '<td valign="top">So some big problems... there was nothing to indicate that this was meant to be... a captured moment I guess we could call it. The sweat, dirt, sawdust, etc, are all way too subtle to know off hand what is going on. Something with him in action, like you said possibly with a tool would have done this shot wonders.<br/> <br/>As it is now, there is no context and no way of knowing that this wasn''t an image where you really went out and tried to get a proper portraite and just failed. (which is how it appears).<br/> <br/>If you wanted to keep it close up perhaps he could be in action. Wiping sweat of his brow, taking a swig of refreshing water, etc.<br/> <br/>The focus is really soft on the eyes and more in focus on his nose and his skin tone seems a bit off. I might have dulled down the green in the back a bit too.</td>', 'So some big problems... there was nothing to indicate that this was meant to be... a captured moment I guess we could call it. The sweat, dirt, sawdust, etc, are all way too subtle to know off hand what is going on. Something with him in action, like you said possibly with a tool would have done this shot wonders. As it is now, there is no context and no way of knowing that this wasn''t an image where you really went out and tried to get a proper portraite and just failed. (which is how it appears). If you wanted to keep it close up perhaps he could be in action. Wiping sweat of his brow, taking a swig of refreshing water, etc. The focus is really soft on the eyes and more in focus on his nose and his skin tone seems a bit off. I might have dulled down the green in the back a bit too.', '2007-07-26 03:32:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3938553, 553635, 14986, '<td valign="top">Really artistic portrait that I like alot.  A little edgy, but not overdone IMO.</td>', 'Really artistic portrait that I like alot.  A little edgy, but not overdone IMO.', '2007-07-26 03:45:51.000000', NULL, 0),
