(3954924, 555382, 25397, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i> way too dark </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>haha!<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by albc28:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a lovely photo.  I think catching the lghit from behind her instead of in front had a reverse effect.  Your model appears to have some Very gorgeous eyes, wish you could have the light there to bring them out more.  Still a great photo. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>haha!<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kawhona:</b></div><hr/><i> The backlighting on the hair is interesting but, the shadow on the face makes it not work for me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hurhurhur!<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jkkerr:</b></div><hr/><i> needs a bit of fill </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hark. forgive them father, for they no not what they do.<br/> <br/>awersome stuff man</td>', 'Originally posted by eyewave: way too dark   haha! Originally posted by albc28: This is a lovely photo.  I think catching the lghit from behind her instead of in front had a reverse effect.  Your model appears to have some Very gorgeous eyes, wish you could have the light there to bring them out more.  Still a great photo.   haha! Originally posted by kawhona: The backlighting on the hair is interesting but, the shadow on the face makes it not work for me.   hurhurhur! Originally posted by jkkerr: needs a bit of fill   hark. forgive them father, for they no not what they do. awersome stuff man', '2007-08-01 00:37:18.000000', NULL, 0),
